## Root cause
The dispatcher's compile gate (`compile_gate` in `longrun/bin/dispatch360.py`) walks the **whole worktree** and runs `lake env lean <absolute file>` with **cwd = the worktree root**, not `release/`. The root had no `lean-toolchain` and no lakefile, and elan has no configured default toolchain, so all 68 `.lean` files aborted instantly with `error: no default toolchain configured` (exit 1). The authored files were never the problem — the same commands from `release/` exit 0.

## Fix (no `.lean` file touched)
Added a root Lake workspace that shares the `release/` artifacts:
- `lakefile.toml` — minimal root package requiring mathlib (infrastructure only)
- `lean-toolchain`, `lake-manifest.json` — copies of the release versions
- `.lake/packages` → `release/.lake/packages`, `.lake/build/lib/lean` → `release/.lake/build/lib/lean`

